rooms_desc ({"	Your surroundings have totally changed - it is a barren, dusty placewithout life or greenery, baking beneath a hell-red sun. The dusty plainsare broken by three features: huge holes in the earth, great iron fortresses, and a winding black river, undoubtedly the River Styx. This isthe Layer of Pazunia, Palace of 1,001 Closets.","	The smell of rotting jungle vegetations greets you even before youopen the door. You are at the edge of a range of jagged mountains, over-looking a jungle that seems to go on forever. There is a river some milesaway, and a path leading from the door toward it. Beyond the river is amassive city inhabited by over 100,000 demons of all description, and toweringseveral miles high in the center of the great city is an incrediblyornate palace: The Palace of Demogorgon. Shimmering pools of mercury laybefore you in every direction, most likely gates to other layers of theAbyss.","	You have entered the Realm of Feng-Tu, the home of the Chinese godsand goddesses Tou Mu, Goddess of the North Star, and Lu Yueh, God of Epidemics. The realm of Feng-Tu appears as a mighty citadel, Oriental inappearance, that rises up a branch of the Styx called How Nai-ho. Acrossthe river from the mercury pool from which you have exited is the Gate ofthe Demons, Kuei-Men-Kuan, which is large enough to permit elephantine behemoths to pass through easily. ","	You emerge inside an elaborate fortress with marching squads of demonscarrying pull-arms drilling in the halls around the entrance. This is aninfinite castle, the court of millions of demon soldiers drilling constantlyfor war against both Demogorgon and Orcus (and any stray and especiallyannoying Wizzes that manage to find themselves on Saffron's bad side). Themoment you enter, a guard patrol of 100 demons, weapons at the ready, surrounds you, blocking your way. If you ask Saffron nicely, perhaps shewould command her demon battalions to allow you safe passage.","	Two skulls stand guard at the bridge. Their eye sockets gleam, andoccasionally the jaw of one will move. The other then responds, although nosound is audible at this distance. The bridge spans a moat deeper thanany canyon in the Abyss; not water, but fiery lava flares and bubbles in the distant depths, although mostly all you see is the orange glow onthe dark stone sides on the moat. On the far side of the bridge is a massiveblack portcullis, the light of the blood-red sun dancing across its polishedsurface. On the gate's jagged, wicked spikes are impaled the mutilated bodiesof those who have displeased the mistress of this fortress. Some of theirfaces, barely recognizable through the caked blood and hideous wounds belongto such notables as Cirith, Plastic, and Helmut.","	As you approached the portcullis, the enormous gate lifted with analmost terrifying silence, and the strong stench of sulfur and ozone assailedyour nostrels, wafting in from the depths of this evil place. The hugechamber beyond is illuminated by glowing red balls which float near thehigh ceiling. The room is circular, with thick stone columns of purealabaster lining the outer wall. In the center, four stairways lead up toa vast platform, shaped in a circle concentric to the walls of the room. Inthe very center of the room, a vast pillar fashioned from the purest copper,rises from the floor to the ceiling nearly 200 feet away.","	As you ascend the serpent-like stairway, you enter a room whichtowers over every other point in sight - including the mountains visible tothe farthest horizon. The walls and ceiling are formed by a shimmering greendome - transparent, but somehow appearing solid. The dominant feature of theroom is the dais that towers in the middle, topped by an enormous throne. Thethrone seems to have been made from the skulls of all types of creatures.One corner of the room is devoted to massive banquet tables, loaded withplates and dishes of great finery, each which holds some kind of exoticfood. Along the edge of the platform, opposite the banquet tables, thrivesa lush garden of bizarre plants. Many of these are blossoms of exquisitebeauty, but others are gap-toothed horros that seem to sniff and snap at anything around them. Before the throne is a wide, silver pool. Theliquid in it appears to be water, but it is unnaturally still.","	Stepping into the pool of silver water, you suddenly feel yourselffalling, and you retch repeatedly since it feels very much like you havebeen twisted inside out. Without warning, you land with a bone-jarring*thump* to behold the depths of Hell itself. Horrible screams echo throughthe cavernous chamber as you look out over a long, narrow lake filled withboiling lava. Demons with pitchforks jab at pitiful wailing people trying toescape the awful, eternal pain. As you look closer, you realize with agasp of horror that...oh my God...do you see yourself in that pool? You some-how get the feeling that to cross the Princess of Hell (Saffron, of course),you may very well spend time here until the end of days.",0,0,})
rooms_short ({"Welcome to the Abyss.","The Realm of Demogorgon","The Realm of Feng-Tu","The Palace of Graz'zt","The bridge.","Chamber of the Princely Guard","Throne Room","The Lake of Fire",0,0,})
